<html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{max-width:1150px;margin:35px auto;font:17px Georgia;line-height:1.5}td,th{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:6px}table{border-collapse:collapse}img{width:100%}</style><h1>250-episode return to A, B and C</h1><b>EXPLORATORY VALIDATION ONLY; no held-out tests</b><p>Three independent comparisons: A-B-C-D-return A, A-B-C-D-return B, and A-B-C-D-return C. The return simulator starts from the corresponding saved reference state, with frozen final weights. The repeated A-B-C-D prefix is reused from the saved checkpoints; it is not trained a second time on top of D. Original A validation metrics and models are reused exactly. For the new B/C comparisons, replay branches start from the saved ordinary checkpoint immediately after learning B/C and replay only that target through later tasks. Original ordinary checkpoints are reused as the matched no-replay controls. The 250 original episodes and splits are unchanged. No new teacher data are collected. No held-out test trajectories are opened. These additional validation comparisons are exploratory, not independent evidence from new test data. More cases or replay do not guarantee a win.</p><p>Original A replay candidates did not pass every new-task force-adaptation constraint. Their A retention curves are still shown, but are not relabelled as eligible final controllers. B/C eligibility and initial-task tracking quality are also reported. If the controller was inaccurate at learning, poor later tracking alone is not evidence of forgetting. A force-imitation gate is not itself a closed-loop angle-tracking measurement.</p><h2>All validation outcomes</h2><table><tr><th>Task</th><th>Controller</th><th>Attempts</th><th>Completed</th><th>Failed</th><th>Pass</th><th>Mean RMSE deg</th><th>Initial quality</th><th>Adaptation eligible</th></tr><tr><td>A_90</td><td>learned</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0209</td><td>True</td><td>not available</td></tr><tr><td>A_90</td><td>noCL</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>4.9075</td><td>True</td><td>not available</td></tr><tr><td>A_90</td><td>CL_beta_1</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0466</td><td>True</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>A_90</td><td>CL_beta_4</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0810</td><td>True</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>A_90</td><td>CL_beta_16</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>5</td><td>2.7639</td><td>True</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>B_60</td><td>learned</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0231</td><td>True</td><td>not available</td></tr><tr><td>B_60</td><td>noCL</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>3.5560</td><td>True</td><td>not available</td></tr><tr><td>B_60</td><td>CL_beta_1</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>3.8154</td><td>True</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>B_60</td><td>CL_beta_4</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0806</td><td>True</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>B_60</td><td>CL_beta_16</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.1092</td><td>True</td><td>False</td></tr><tr><td>C_30</td><td>learned</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0154</td><td>True</td><td>not available</td></tr><tr><td>C_30</td><td>noCL</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>2.9672</td><td>True</td><td>not available</td></tr><tr><td>C_30</td><td>CL_beta_1</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0172</td><td>True</td><td>True</td></tr><tr><td>C_30</td><td>CL_beta_4</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0192</td><td>True</td><td>True</td></tr><tr><td>C_30</td><td>CL_beta_16</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>6</td><td>0.0170</td><td>True</td><td>True</td></tr></table><img src="FIGURES/summary/all_candidates.png"><img src="FIGURES/architecture/network_and_cost.png"><img src="FIGURES/summary/final_D_tracking.png"><img src="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00.png"><img src="FIGURES/tracking/B_60/beta_1/B_60_A_e50_validation_00.png"><img src="FIGURES/tracking/C_30/beta_1/C_30_A_e50_validation_00.png"><h2>All exported figures</h2><p>Each reference and beta has both a four-panel figure and an angle-only figure. PDF and SVG are vector exports; PNG is for slides. All learning curves are included. Files are indexed in FIGURE_INDEX.csv.</p><ul><li>tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00 — <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00.pdf">PDF</a> | <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00.png">PNG</a> | <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00.svg">SVG</a></li><li>angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00 — <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00.pdf">PDF</a> | <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00.png">PNG</a> | <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e50_validation_00.svg">SVG</a></li><li>tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e60_validation_00 — <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e60_validation_00.pdf">PDF</a> | <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e60_validation_00.png">PNG</a> | <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e60_validation_00.svg">SVG</a></li><li>angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e60_validation_00 — <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e60_validation_00.pdf">PDF</a> | <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e60_validation_00.png">PNG</a> | <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e60_validation_00.svg">SVG</a></li><li>tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e70_validation_00 — <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e70_validation_00.pdf">PDF</a> | <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e70_validation_00.png">PNG</a> | <a href="FIGURES/tracking/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e70_validation_00.svg">SVG</a></li><li>angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e70_validation_00 — <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e70_validation_00.pdf">PDF</a> | <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_90/beta_1/A_90_A_e70_validation_00.png">PNG</a> | <a href="FIGURES/angle_only/A_9